","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"},{"bioguideId":"P000621","fullName":"Rep. Pou, Nellie [D-NJ-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"L000599","fullName":"Rep. Lawler, Michael [R-NY-17]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"M001238","fullName":"Rep. McBride, Sarah [D-DE-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"DE"},{"bioguideId":"B001257","fullName":"Rep. Bilirakis, Gus M. [R-FL-12]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T21:57:03+00:00","id":"hr4231-119","introducedDate":"2025-06-27","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-27","text":"Referred to the Committee on Energy and Commerce, and in addition to the Committee on Ways and Means, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"laws":[],"number":"4231","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Health","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"K000376","district":16,"fullName":"Rep. Kelly, Mike [R-PA-16]","party":"R","state":"PA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-06-27","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Treat and Reduce Obesity Act of </strong><strong>2025</strong></p><p>This bill expands Medicare coverage of intensive behavioral therapy for obesity. Specifically, the bill allows coverage for therapy that is provided by (1) a physician who is not a primary care physician; or&nbsp;(2) other health care providers (e.g., physician assistants and nurse practitioners) and approved counseling programs, if provided upon a referral from, and in coordination with, a physician or primary care practitioner. Currently, such therapy is covered only if provided by a primary care practitioner.</p><p>The bill also allows coverage under Medicare's prescription drug benefit of drugs used for the treatment of obesity or for weight loss management for individuals who are overweight.</p>","updateDate":"2025-08-05T21:33:15Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Treat and Reduce Obesity Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-01T08:06:04Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-01T08:06:04Z"}
